From: ARLinux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] util: do not count failed singleton construction as an acquire

DxvkInstance construction can throw when no Vulkan adapter supports the
required features. Chromium retries CreateDXGIFactory in the same process.
Incrementing the use count before construction leaves a null singleton with
a nonzero count, so the next factory dereferences a null instance instead of
returning the original initialization failure.

Only count successful acquisitions. No adapter features are fabricated.

diff --git a/src/util/util_singleton.h b/src/util/util_singleton.h
--- a/src/util/util_singleton.h
+++ b/src/util/util_singleton.h
@@ -20,9 +20,10 @@ public:
   Rc<T> acquire(Args... constantArgs) {
     std::lock_guard lock(m_mutex);
 
-    if (!(m_useCount++))
+    if (!m_useCount)
       m_object = new T(constantArgs...);
 
+    ++m_useCount;
     return m_object;
   }
 
